WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.002
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome to

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.972
"The Tonight Show," everybody!
We are here!

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.241
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ready to make you laugh!

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.342
Thank you for watching.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.044
Thank you for being here,
everybody.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.445
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.814
Well, guys,
Thanksgiving is behind us,

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.584
but today was another
very big day.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.152
-It's Cyber Monday, guys.
-It is Cyber Monday.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:23.256
-Record Cyber Monday sales.
-Cyber Monday is on track

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:26.091
to be the biggest
online sales day in history,

00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:30.329
with shoppers shelling out
up to $12.7 billion today.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:33.699
-Yep, today, Americans spent
billions shopping online,

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.369
or as that's known in 2020,
every day.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.737
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.906
Seriously, the whole year
has been Cyber Monday.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:43.709
At this point, all UPS guys are
built like Dwayne Johnson.

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.178
"Where do you want this couch?"

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.646
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:49.449
There's deals on everything.
There's nose-hair trimmers,

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.650
scuba equipment, lingerie,
and, right now,

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.652
there's an Amazon worker loading
them all into the same box,

00:00:53.652 --> 00:00:56.755
going, "What is your life?"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.755 --> 00:00:59.125
I saw that the jewelry store
Jared was offering

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.895
up to 50% off storewide.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.396
Though it's kind of weird
telling your girlfriend,

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.632
"He went to Jared --
on Cyber Monday."

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.733
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.168
Some political news.
On Sunday morning,

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.771
President Trump did his first
post-election TV interview

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.273
with Maria Bartiromo
on Fox News.

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.675
It lasted 46 minutes,
and I'm getting the sense

00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:18.310
he's not quite over
the election.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.512
Listen to this.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.648
-Mr. President, thank you
very much for being here.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.093
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.461
-Even the biggest Trump
supporters were like,

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:36.862
"Maybe we should let
Rudy Giuliani

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:37.964
talk about this instead.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.667
He's been handling this
pretty well."

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.669
[ Imitating droplets splashing ]

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.971
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.073
-Hey.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.908
-It started
as a conspiracy theory

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.776
about election fraud
and turned into a commercial

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:53.946
for the Squatty Potty.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:56.282
Yeah, I was worried that the end
of Trump's presidency

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.917
might get embarrassing,
but at least he's

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.820
only on national TV saying,
"Big massive dumps."

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.655
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:03.957
Meanwhile,
at the White House today,

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.658
Melania Trump
unveiled the Christmas --

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.493
the official
Christmas decorations.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:08.261
Take a look.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:18.271
♪♪

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.738
♪♪

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:21.674
[ Laughter ]
-Why do they keep putting

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.776
Melania in charge of the
Christmas decorations?

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:26.479
We know
she doesn't like doing it.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.548
Do you want to hear
the leaked audio again?

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.719
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:36.089
Don't put Melania in charge
if she doesn't want to do it!

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.391
[ Applause ]

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.592
Make it fun!

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.627
Put Rudy Giuliani
in charge of this.

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:44.063
He'll have a Santa leaking
eggnog from his side burns.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.698
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:49.235
Put Jared Kushner on the shelf,
change his position every day.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:54.374
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:57.076
Melania made him have
two middle fingers.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.178
Have Mike Pence do it.
He's so white,

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.648
he's just a top hat and a pipe
away from being the new Frosty.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.549
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.852
But this year's gingerbread
White House is incredible.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.387
It features more than
400 pounds of dough

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.690
and a gingerbread man
who refuses to leave.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.159
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.627
Trump must love the decorations,

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.496
because he's used a tiny
gingerbread Oval Office desk

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.032
in his last press conference.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.332
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:22.268
Did you see that?
What is he doing?

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.403
Is that a desk?
Or is that the tiny table

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:26.439
that separates the pizza
from the box?

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.942
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.777
And here's some news
about the President-elect.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.579
Over the weekend,
Joe Biden ran into

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.514
a little trouble
while playing with his dog.

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.416
Listen to this.
-The President-elect,

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:39.519
he spent Sunday night
at the doctor's office

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.988
after twisting his ankle
playing with his dog.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:44.056
Biden's doctor says,
after a CT scan,

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:47.059
he ended up with hairline
fractures in his right foot.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:50.062
He'll probably have to be
in a boot for a little while.

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.363
-Biden was like,
"Ah, it's no big deal.

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:54.067
I've been dealing with a
fractured hairline for years."

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.437
When the news broke,
Kamala Harris was stretching

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.572
in the bullpen like,
"I guess I'm getting in the game

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:02.342
sooner than I thought."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:05.010
"Ooh! Let's go."
I feel bad for Biden, though.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.047
Nobody wants to start a new job
in a walking boot.

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.815
It's hard to act tough
with China when you have to

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:12.584
leave a press conference
on one of those knee scooters.

00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:18.591
[ Laughter ]
[ Bell ringing ]

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.994
I couldn't -- I don't know how
to make the space work work.

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:24.864
You know, those things.
[ Bell ringing ]

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.132
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.000
♪♪

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.069
[ Bell ringing continues ]
No, okay.

00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:33.372
Hey, here's a big -- a big sp--
Here's a burg?

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.174
Here's a burg.
Here's a burger for you.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.608
Who else wants a burger?
-A burger, I want a burger.

00:04:36.608 --> 00:04:38.711
-Anybody else want a burger?
-Give me a burger.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.647
-Burger, burger, burger, burger,
burger, burger, no problem.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.816
Oh, here's a big sports story
for you here.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:47.353
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.754
You love sports,
don't you, Tariq?

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:50.723
-Uh, pretty much no.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.692
-Well, here's one for you.
The Denver Broncos had to face

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:56.896
the New Orleans Saints without
any of their quarterbacks.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.197
Watch this.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.566
-In Denver, practice squad
receiver Kendall Hinton

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.201
got the start for the Broncos

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.636
after all of the team's
quarterbacks

00:05:04.636 --> 00:05:07.640
were disqualified
over coronavirus concerns.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.942
-The Broncos lost, 31-3.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:13.379
Hinton completed
just one pass, overall.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.813
-Oh, man.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:17.249
Yeah, the NFL saw the Oscars
go without a host and said,

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:19.085
"We can top that."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:22.655
Yeah, the Broncos played without
a quarterback and lost, 31-3.

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:25.124
Even more upsetting, the Jets
had their starting quarterback

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:28.894
and still lost just as bad.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:30.896
Listen to this.
Tecate beer,

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:34.533
which is made in Holland --
Did you know that?

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:36.102
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:38.270
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.906
It is made in Holland,
so it's now facing a lawsuit

00:05:40.906 --> 00:05:43.743
for posing as a Mexican beer.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.378
Tough year
for fans of Mexican beer.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:47.780
You got fake Tecate
or you got Corona.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.282
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:52.017
Some entertainment news.
I saw that Netflix

00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:53.619
is being pressured
by the British government

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.055
to put a disclaimer
on "The Crown,"

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:59.158
saying that it's fictional.
Yeah.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:01.527
They also want everyone to know
that Helena Bonham Carter

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:03.429
is not actually
the Queen's sister.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.064
She's an actress.

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:07.366
And also, you see those credits
you see rolling at the end?

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:10.803
Doesn't happen in real life.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:15.674
It's what they call a TV show.

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:16.976
I don't know
what to make of this.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.777
In a new interview,
George Clooney revealed

00:06:18.777 --> 00:06:20.646
some interesting information
about how he cuts his hair.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:21.881
Watch this.

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.882
-I've been cutting my own hair
for 25 years.

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:29.021
So, years ago, I bought a --
a thing called a Flowbee.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.122
It comes with a vacuum cleaner
and the clippers?

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:31.824
-Yes!
-Yeah. I still have it.

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:34.594
My haircuts
take literally two minutes.

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:36.662
I go --
-Is this -- Is this Flowbee?

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:37.596
-Yeah, it's Flowbee.

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:40.666
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:42.168
-No.
-No.

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:43.302
-If you think that's crazy,

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:44.970
I heard he manscapes
with a Slap Chop.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:48.908
[ Laughter ]
That's what I heard.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:50.843
And, finally, I saw that Oreo
is now selling

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:53.845
a cookie-scented candle
on their Website.

00:06:53.845 --> 00:06:55.648
I'm already excited
for tomorrow's headline --

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:58.317
"Florida man rushed to ER
after eating lit candle."

00:06:58.317 --> 00:06:59.485
Happy Thanksgiving.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:00.720
I hope everybody
had a nice Thanksgiving.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.755
Did you -- Did you --
Did you spatchcock?

00:07:03.755 --> 00:07:05.057
-I did.
-You did?

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:06.459
-Yeah.
-How did it turn out?

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:08.093
-Best turkey
I've ever made, man.

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:10.262
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
-I mean, yeah.

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:11.697
-Because you've talked
the talk before.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:14.133
-I have,
but I walk the walk, as well.

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:15.934
-Yeah, but usually
you spatchcock

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.503
and then
you throw it on the grill.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:19.472
-Yeah, but -- Yeah,
I didn't grill this time.

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:22.074
Well, I spatchcocked it,
I put it on the grill,

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:25.210
but just the oven grill.
Like not outside, like on the --

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.945
-Yeah, on the barbecue grill.
-Yeah, no.

00:07:26.945 --> 00:07:28.080
-But is it better than that,
even?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.982
-Better.
Better than anything ever.

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:32.051
-Spatchcock is the --
You butterfly the turkey.

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:33.986
-Yeah.
-Yeah, you take the backbone.

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:36.021
-I just told you that
Thursday, right?

00:07:36.021 --> 00:07:37.856
-No, last year, you told me.
-Oh, yeah.

00:07:37.856 --> 00:07:39.091
-Yeah, yeah, I mean --
Whatever.

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:40.359
I don't really
pay attention to you.

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:43.028
[ Laughter ]
When -- When --

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:44.262
The night I texted --

00:07:44.262 --> 00:07:46.365
My assistant reads me the texts
that you send.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:49.902
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:51.136
No, you told me
you were the doing that,

00:07:51.136 --> 00:07:52.638
but I was like,
"Oh, did you really do it?"

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.139
You went for it.
-Yeah. It was awesome.

00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:59.278
-Yeah. It was a -- it was a fun
Thanksgiving, I think, for us.

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:02.682
I mean, we got invited to do the
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:04.350
We got invited to -- oh.
Yeah.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.618
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:08.020
Which is an honor just to even
be invited there.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.322
But then we got asked to open

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:10.956
the Macy's Thanksgiving Day
Parade,

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:14.393
which is unbelievable.
We were so excited about that.

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:18.364
We got -- I got here around
6:40, 6:30, something like that.

00:08:18.364 --> 00:08:20.433
And it was
raining cats and dogs.

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:21.767
I go, "Oh, man."

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:24.269
Already, the idea of pulling off
a parade is tough.

00:08:24.269 --> 00:08:28.807
But to do it during a rain
is just gonna be insane.

00:08:28.807 --> 00:08:32.211
But we got there.
They did a great job --

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:35.180
NBC, also New York City
did a great job.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.582
Thank you, Bill de Blasio,

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:38.484
for even letting it happen
and do it.

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:42.655
It made a lot of people happy.
So, we were in the Macy's --

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:44.757
Actually in the department store
for the first time.

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:46.358
-Yeah.
-That was our holding --

00:08:46.358 --> 00:08:48.227
-That was our dressing room.
-It was so bizarre.

00:08:48.227 --> 00:08:50.262
Our dressing room was in Macy's.

00:08:50.262 --> 00:08:52.698
It was all dolled up for
Christmas and all that stuff.

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:54.333
And we were practicing
the dancing.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.335
It was like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:58.637
And we got to perform live,
which we never get to do.

00:08:58.637 --> 00:09:00.806
-Yeah.
-Because if you're on the float,

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:02.241
there's no way you can
mic those things,

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:04.443
so you have to, like,
lip-sync to a track.

00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:06.913
Which sometimes works
and sometimes doesn't.

00:09:06.913 --> 00:09:08.180
There was one year,
it was so cold,

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.115
I couldn't even move my lips.
-Yeah, wow.

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:12.184
-It was like -- yeah.
But it was wild.

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:16.121
And again, I want to thank our
choreographer, Sarah O'Gleby,

00:09:16.121 --> 00:09:18.190
who always is just --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.359
She is so talented.

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:22.761
And made it so fun.
I love that.

00:09:22.761 --> 00:09:26.432
It was -- It was definitely
a memorable Thanksgiving.

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:27.833
But happy we got to do that

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:30.135
and make a lot of people laugh
and smile.

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:32.305
But another thing happened
on Thanksgiving --

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:34.673
the dog show,
the national dog show.

00:09:34.673 --> 00:09:36.742
-Mm.
-Yeah. You watch that?

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:37.944
-Of course.
-Yeah, of course.

00:09:37.944 --> 00:09:40.412
There was
a very interesting dog there.

00:09:40.412 --> 00:09:41.913
Check this out.

00:09:41.913 --> 00:09:45.050
-Here's the Miniature
American Shepherd.

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:48.053
This dog is named
Love that Jimmy Fallon.

00:09:48.053 --> 00:09:50.322
Said they named him Jimmy
because of his high energy

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:52.758
and goofy personality.
There you go, Jimmy.

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:54.759
[ Laughter ]
-Wait. What?

00:09:54.759 --> 00:09:58.497
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:00.366
That's real?
-That's real.

00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:01.567
-What's up with --

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:04.536
-"Love that Jimmy Fallon"
was the name of that dog.

00:10:04.536 --> 00:10:06.872
-Yeah, man, he's got
a goofy personality, so...

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:09.041
[ Laughter ]
What else you gonna call him?

00:10:09.041 --> 00:10:11.043
-Yeah, well --
No, I mean -- Well, he's a

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:16.382
Miniature American Shepherd,
from Denton, Texas,

00:10:16.382 --> 00:10:17.649
which is outside of Dallas.

00:10:17.649 --> 00:10:19.284
But I was looking at the dog.

00:10:19.284 --> 00:10:20.519
You know,
'cause I watch these things,

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:23.189
and honestly,
a flawless physical specimen...

